# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CSR — .gitignore   (track source; not build outputs, caches, or personal data)
#
# NOTE: git does NOT support a trailing comment on a pattern line. "foo.json # why"
# is read as a filename containing " # why" and silently matches nothing. Every
# comment here is therefore on its own line. This file previously had two inline
# comments, which is how csr_archive.json and sc_images.json — both personal — came
# within one commit of a public repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Build / generated artifacts (rebuilt from source — don't commit)
dist/
build/
release/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
CSR.html
sc_stats.html
CSR-v*.zip
csr_icon.png

# Per-user runtime data & caches
CSR-data/
csr_config.json
# each user's accumulated session archive — personal play history
csr_archive.json
# each user's own ship/gun art cache (~9 MB, fetched per install)
sc_images.json

# Per-user online caches: these hold YOUR handle, citizen record and org
sc_profile.json
sc_online.json
# per-death records from the deprecated live analyzer
diviner.json

# Personal Star Citizen logs — never publish these
Game.log
*.log
logbackups/
# a friend's logs, shared for testing — not ours to publish
Zephyrion Logs/

# Third-party tool kept locally for reference — not ours to redistribute
StarLogs-v0.9.1/

# Local machine config written by editors and dev tooling — absolute paths and
# per-machine permissions, never portable to anyone else's checkout
**/settings.local.json

# Internal working notes — architecture, open TODOs, notes-to-self. Kept local.
HANDOFF.md
# Drafts of announcement / Discord copy, staged here before posting. Underscore
# prefix marks anything that is written for a person, not for the repo.
/_*.txt
/_*.md

# OS / editor cruft
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KEPT (intentionally NOT ignored) so `build_exe.bat` bundles them and a fresh
# clone builds an exe with data ready (delete-to-refetch still works):
#   sc_ship_matrix.json   sc_item_names.json   sc_blueprints.json   sc_fonts_embed.css   csr.ico
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.claude/
